Z||000000||maninblack||11-19-2000||02:38 AM||||I was picking up from a red lite and just about shifting from 2nd to 3rd,I felt somthing weird from the clutch and when I engaged 3rd,the car died.I rolled it to a stop on the shoulder,shut it off and cranked<BR>it again,nothing happen.It will crank over but not start.Tried it a few more times,all <BR>it sounds like it no fuel going into the engine.I should have half a tank of gas left<BR>,according to the fuel gauge (its not that<BR>acurate but according to the trip meter,there<BR>ahould be enough gas),it was too dark to check anything under the hood.I tow it to my friends garage and have to wait till monday<BR>now to see whats wrong.However,any of you have the same experiance that can share with me.It's an 87 v6 5sp se and I already have new plugs and stuffs in it.<BR>thx||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wolfhound||11-19-2000||08:09 AM||||Sounds like it could be the ignition module. Check for fire.<BR> It may even crank, on occasion they will work for a short time, when they cool, after failing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DavidHenshaw||11-19-2000||11:51 AM||||Check todays post titled "no spark", sounds like a similar problem.<P>My car had plenty of gas like yours but it was an ignition problem. Ususally start by checking the ignition module, it can be tested by your local auto supply store. Next would be checking the coil, the plug wires, the rotor inside the distributor and then the distributor itself.<P>Dave<P>86 GT fastback||||reg||1
